  "review": [
    "Reviewed the selected account-retention and HEK navigation diffs, relevant request/response handlers and focused tests. Ordinary signed-in profiles can request their own magnetic bundles, research records and evidence packages; explicit retention remains distinct from selecting, preparing or reopening content.",
    "Expected profile and exact record/package IDs, response claim-boundary flags and replay verification remain in the existing paths. Account events retire in-flight UI operations and clear retained selections. Server account/quota gates remain independent of client visibility.",
    "Local repository inputs remain a separate developer feature. Reproduced an explicit-lock precedence defect: a developer account listing the feature still requested local products when locked_features also denied it. Added a negative lock check without restricting ordinary owner catalogs.",
    "HEK references now retain bounded names and declared media types through the existing shared normalizer. HTTP(S) navigation links use noopener/noreferrer and remain labeled as unverified destinations/content/revisions. No external link or provider was fetched during this review.",
    "Scientific data, observation/operator models, hash contracts and certificates are unchanged. Existing diagnostic, fixture, covariance, provenance and no-admission labels remain. Source UI tests are not evidence of a solver result or scientific admission."
